# Installed by PanelAlpha.
#
# mw-config/ is MediaWiki's web installer, and it is first-visitor-wins.
# mw-config/index.php:20 defines MW_CONFIG_CALLBACK before including
# WebStart.php, which is how it runs *without* loading LocalSettings.php at
# all; it then hands the request to WebInstaller, whose page sequence
# (WebInstaller.php:70) is Language, ExistingWiki, Welcome, DBConnect,
# Upgrade, DBSettings, Name, Options, Install, Complete.
#
# WebInstallerExistingWiki::execute() is the only thing between a stranger and
# that sequence: it returns 'skip' outright when
# Installer::getExistingLocalSettings() finds no settings file
# (WebInstallerExistingWiki.php:20-22), and otherwise asks for $wgUpgradeKey.
# On an account that has just been handed a public HTTPS name, a form on the
# open internet that creates a wiki and its bureaucrat is not something to
# leave to an upgrade key.
#
# This wiki was installed from the deploy instead, by MediaWiki's own
# `maintenance/run.php install` running in the container before Apache bound,
# and `maintenance/run.php update` runs on every deploy after that -- so
# nothing that mw-config/ does is still needed here. Deleting the directory is
# what upstream's INSTALL file tells an administrator to do at this point; it
# is denied rather than deleted so that a `git pull` does not quietly bring it
# back.
Require all denied
Satisfy All
